ecision, and perhaps suggest provisional vote for C because crew cooperation is crucial, but we need to confirm stress resilience.\n\nWe need to state a vote. We can choose Candidate C as provisional, explaining why we think crew cooperation and decision quality outweigh B's uncooperative behavior, but we need stress resilience evidence. Or we could stay with B but ask for more info.\n\nGiven the guidelines: \"Do not overvalue one impressive strength while ignoring serious concerns on other safety-relevant criteria.\" B's uncooperative is serious. C's lack of stress resilience evidence is also serious. So we need to weigh.\n\nWe could say: I am leaning toward Candidate C because crew cooperation and decision quality are critical, and his attention skills are excellent, but we need evidence on his stress resilience before final. So provisional vote for C, pending stress resilience info.\n\nThus we will state recommendation for Candidate C, explain reasoning, reference prior discussion, and ask for stress resilience observations for C (and maybe D). Provide evidence: positive atmosphere, correct decisions quickly, excellent attention, puts concern for others above everything. Contrast with B's uncooperative behavior and pretentiousness. Mention missing stress resilience.\n\nNow produce public message and metadata JSON with vote Candidate C."}
